\"size\": 20034, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:06\", \"token_count\": 7244, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-06]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Use sync.Map and atomics for fixed bucket histograms (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go#7474)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7474  \\n\\n**Author**: dashpole  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-08T14:31:21Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-11T16:56:31Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-11T16:56:04Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `optimize_syncmap_histogram` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +560 / -201 across 7 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nImplement a lockless histogram using atomics, and use a sync.Map for attribute access.  This improves performance by ~2x.\\n\\nThe design is very similar to https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7427, but with one additional change to make the histogram data point itself atomic:\\n\\n* For cumulative histograms, which do not use a hot/cold limitedSyncMap, we use a hot/cold data point.  This way, we maintain the keys in the sync map, but still ensure that collection gets a consistent view of measure() calls.\\n\\nParallel benchmarks:\\n\\n```\\n\\n                                                                       │  main.txt   │              hist.txt              │\\n\\n                                                                       │   sec/op    │   sec/op     vs base               │\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsDisabled/Int64Histogram/Attributes/10-24     274.5n ± 2%   125.2n ± 5%  -54.42% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\nSyncMeasure/NoView/ExemplarsDisabled/Float64Histogram/Attributes/10-24   274.1n ± 2%   132.5n ± 2%  -51.65% (p=0.002 n=6)\\n\\ngeomean                                                                  274.3n        128.8n       -53.05%\\n\\n```\\n\\nzero memory allocations before and after this change for Measure().  Omitted for brevity\\n\\nBenchmarks for collect:\\n\\n```\\n\\n                                                    │   main.txt    │               hist.txt               │\\n\\n                                                    │    sec/op     │    sec/op     vs base                │\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 06 pull request use sync map and atom for fix bucket histogram open telemetri opentelemetri go 7474 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7474 author dashpol creat 2025 10 08t14 31 21z updat 2025 12 11t16 56 31z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 11t16 56 04z branch optim _ syncmap _ histogram main chang 560 201 across 7 file label mileston v1 400 descript implement a lockless histogram use atom and use a sync map for attribut access this improv perform by 2x the design is veri similar to http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go pull 7427 but with one addit chang to make the histogram data point itself atom for cumul histogram which do not use a hot cold limitedsyncmap we use a hot cold data point this way we maintain the key in the sync map but still ensur that collect get a consist view of measur call parallel benchmark main txt hist txt sec op sec op v base syncmeasur noview exemplarsdis int64histogram attribut 1024 274 5n 2 125 2n 5 54 42 p 0 002 n 6 syncmeasur noview exemplarsdis float64histogram attribut 1024 274 1n 2 132 5n 2 51 65 p 0 002 n 6 geomean 274 3n 128 8n 53 05 zero memori alloc befor and after this chang for measur omit for breviti benchmark for collect main txt hist txt sec op sec op v base\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875d9f208a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"id\": \"432d9a43e09b