han or equal to val no updat to minimum is made if the current extremum alreadi contain a maximum greater than or equal to val no updat to maximum is made func e extremum n updat val n extremum n if e set e min val e max val\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875d9f208a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"id\": \"a3246858fc4bc1e2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.4234570527735012, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.2882119625335732, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73902893, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875d9f208a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7474.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 32141, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:06\", \"token_count\": 11686, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"Not sure why coverage is failing\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-12-09T16:57:34Z\\n\\n> Not sure why coverage is failing\\n\\nI think the changes are just exposing an area where we have had coverage overlap. I think this has more to do with how we merge coverage instead of the changes here.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**MrAlias** — 2025-12-09T17:10:55Z\\n\\nLikely worth looking into using [Go 1.20 coverage directory feature](https://go.dev/doc/go1.20#cover) to replace our current approach.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dashpole** — 2025-12-11T16:49:43Z\\n\\nSeems to have resolved itself.  Now just links are failing (503s from github due to outage).\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-06]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Use sync.Map an